<title>JAPAN: Japan's Ex-Im Bank co-finances loan to Philippines.</title>
<headline>Japan's Ex-Im Bank co-finances loan to Philippines.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Export-Import Bank of Japan said on Monday that it along with six Japanese commercial banks will lend the Philippine government 20.8 billion yen to help build and repair roads.</p>
<p>The Ex-Im Bank said in a statement that it will lend 70 percent of the total, or 14.6 billion yen, with the rest coming from commercial banks, led by Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi.</p>
<p>The loan is part of a co-financing scheme with the Asian Development Bank, which totals $167 million, it said.</p>
<p>&quot;The country (the Philippines) lags behind other ASEAN countries in road construction, and this has been a great impediment to its economic development,&quot; the Ex-Im Bank said.</p>
</text>
